From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Badis Meddouri <meddouri.badis@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:52:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: create mShowKeyguardWakeLock on demand on Android TV

On devices without a keyguard (Android TV), CentralSurfaces is never
instantiated, so KeyguardViewMediator.registerCentralSurfaces() and therefore
setupLocked() never run and mShowKeyguardWakeLock stays null.

PhoneWindowManager.systemReady() still calls into KeyguardService, which
forwards onSystemReady() to the mediator. That reaches doKeyguardLocked() ->
showLocked(), which dereferences the null wake lock:

  java.lang.NullPointerException: Attempt to invoke virtual method
  'void android.os.PowerManager$WakeLock.acquire()' on a null object reference
      at ...keyguard.KeyguardViewMediator.showLocked(KeyguardViewMediator.java:19)
      at ...keyguard.KeyguardViewMediator.doKeyguardLocked(KeyguardViewMediator.java:300)
      at ...keyguard.KeyguardViewMediator$12.handleMessage(KeyguardViewMediator.java:104)

The NPE is on the SystemUI main thread, so SystemUI crash-loops from the
start of boot. The visible symptom is a black screen: the window manager has
FallbackHome as the focused activity, but its window never gets a surface
(mHasSurface=false isReadyForDisplay()=false), so nothing is ever drawn and
screencap returns an all-black frame.

This is the same class of bug as the null CentralSurfaces dereference in
StatusBarKeyguardViewManager, and the same fix: create the wake lock lazily
instead of assuming the phone code path ran.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
@@ -2123,6 +2123,15 @@ public class KeyguardViewMediator implements RemoteInputController.Callback
     private void showLocked(Bundle options) {
         Trace.beginSection("KeyguardViewMediator#showLocked acquiring mShowKeyguardWakeLock");
         if (DEBUG) Log.d(TAG, "showLocked");
+        // On devices without a keyguard (e.g. Android TV) CentralSurfaces is never
+        // created, so registerCentralSurfaces()/setupLocked() never runs and
+        // mShowKeyguardWakeLock is still null. Create it on demand instead of
+        // crashing SystemUI, which would take the whole UI down.
+        if (mShowKeyguardWakeLock == null) {
+            mShowKeyguardWakeLock = mPM.newWakeLock(PowerManager.PARTIAL_WAKE_LOCK,
+                    "show keyguard");
+            mShowKeyguardWakeLock.setReferenceCounted(false);
+        }
         // ensure we stay awake until we are finished displaying the keyguard
         mShowKeyguardWakeLock.acquire();
         mLastShowRequest++;
--
